{
 "regions": {
  "r2": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "84. A mouse, gnawing a hole into a basket, at night, fell",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "into the mouth of a serpent that, with its body pent up in a",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "basket and its limbs weakened by starvation, had grown",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "despondent. Filled with its meat the serpent quickly glided",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "away through the same opening ( lit. the same passage, viz.",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "the hole made by the mouse ); see, my men, it is destiny",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "alone that is the cause of the rise and fall of men.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r3": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "85. A ball, though struck on the ground with a blow",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "from the hand, does rebound upwards; generally the misfor-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "tunes of the virtuous are not everlasting ( are temporary ).",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r4": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "86. Sloth is a dreadfull enemy abiding in the body of",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "man; there is no friend like industriousness by resorting to",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "which a man is never ruined.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r5": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "87. A tree. though cut down, grows again; the moon,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "though waned, waxes again; thus reflecting good men are",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "not troubled in this world, when plunged in misery.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r6": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "88. Indra was worsted in battle by his enemies, though",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "possessed of greatness and prowess—even he who had Bṛhas-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "pati for his adviser, the thunderbolt for his weapon, the gods",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "for his soldiers, and the heaven for his citadel; he verily",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "enjoyed the favour of Hari ( Vishnu ), and had Airàvata for",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "his elephant; it is clear, then, that it is better to submit to",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "fate; oh, fie ! valour is useless.",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r7": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "89. The fruit which men get depends on action ( done in",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "a former life), and the inducement to action is in consonance",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "with it ( action done in a previous life ); still a wise man",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "should be doing a thing only after mature consideration.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r8": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "90. A bald man, scorched on the head by the rays of the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "sun and wishing for a shady place, went to ( rest under ) a",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "palm tree; even there, a big fruit falling ( from the tree )",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "broke his pate with a crash. Verily misfortunes do, indeed,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "go there where a luckless man goes.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r1": {
   "type": "page_number",
   "lines": [
    {
